The target is Euclid’s algorithm. I’m normalizing both inputs with `abs` so the implementation covers all integers (including negative inputs) and returns the conventional nonnegative gcd; the main proof obligation will be universal rather than just replaying the two examples. The key technical point is expressing the loop invariant in a form the supplied semantics and SMT backend can discharge without altering the reference files.
