codex
The first symbolic attempt exposed two real proof-engineering issues rather than a program bug: unconstrained frame maps caused irrelevant closure-cell branches, and the backend does not automatically derive Euclid’s divisibility lemma through nested modulo terms. I’ve eliminated the spurious state branches; I’m now isolating the arithmetic lemma so it is either proved once and reused or replaced by an explicit executable gcd specification, rather than silently assuming it in the program theorem.
apply patch
patch: completed
